    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1194">

                <pb facs="0849" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/17.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador Wilson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. Department has received from American Consul, Nogales, notice that
                    insurrectionary forces are collecting taxes on mines and other property.
                    Department is advising Consulate as follows: [Quotes telegram to Consul
                    Simpich.]</p>
                <p>You will bring this matter immediately to the attention of the appropriate
                    authorities in the sense indicated in the instruction to the Consul.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
